# THE BUILD SCRIPTS MUST KEEP LF IN THE WORKING TREE.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so a checkout hands every text file
# CRLF -- and bash cannot run a script with CRLF line endings. It does not fail
# on the carriage returns themselves; it reports
#     build-ti.sh: line 37: syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''
# which reads as a broken script rather than as a line-ending problem, and it
# happens after any fresh checkout rather than after an edit, so nothing in the
# session points at the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The CVBasic sources and the generated assembly are read by Cygwin tools for
# the same reason.
*.bas text eol=lf
